codex
The deliverables are internally consistent and contain no credential material. The final repository profile resolves to Track B / algebra / integer lattice / linear algebra / exact symbolic / native / no reduction, and the planted witness verifies even after removing `inst["answer"]`, confirming the checker does not consult the hidden solution. One tooling caveat is now documented by the evidence itself: all required transcript calls are HTTP 403 errors and therefore correctly count as 0 scored attempts, not model failures.
The paper audit, module, README, and all local verification gates are complete. The required external hardening and G9 oracle runs cannot produce scored attempts because the configured OpenRouter key has limit_remaining=0; the script-owned error transcripts are retained and documented rather than misreported as failures.
  ✓ Read the full paper/source and triage native problem families against G/H/V and Track A/B
  ✓ Inspect repository interfaces and implement the generator or document a justified rejection
  → Run self-tests, adversary measurements, and hardening/G9 harnesses as applicable
  ✓ Write all required deliverables and verify repository submission checks
