631:In \cite{GMO}, moduli spaces of rational tropical covers of a line are constructed as balanced polyhedral complexes in a surrounding vector space. The approach taken there is different from ours, although also motivated by tropical intersection theory. The moduli spaces are constructed by gluing pieces using tropical intersection theory, respectively by interpreting them as a marked polyhedral subcomplex of the moduli space of rational curves. The methods used in \cite{GMO} highly rely on the genus to be zero and cannot be easily generalized to arbitrary genus. 
