The paper’s native search objects are clearer now: a cover is a weighted metric graph mapping to the three-rayed tropical line, with integral slopes, local balancing, Riemann–Hurwitz inequalities, and prescribed end-weight partitions. I’m now checking whether reconstruction from branch data has a paper-backed hard regime, or whether the paper instead reduces every fixed combinatorial type to linear equations—which would force an honest Track B treatment or rejection.
