\begin{definition}\label{defn:automorphism}
 Let $h:\Gamma \rightarrow \tilde \Gamma$ be a cover. An \emph{automorphism} of
a cover $h:\Gamma \rightarrow \tilde \Gamma$ is an isomorphism $\phi:\Gamma\rightarrow\Gamma$, s.t. $\phi\circ h=h$. We
denote by $\Aut(h)$ the group of automorphisms of $h:\Gamma \rightarrow \tilde \Gamma$.
\end{definition}




We will focus our attention on covers of a tropical line in the tropical projective plane. To fix notation, we define:
\begin{definition}
Consider the abstract curve $\CL$ of a tropical line in the tropical projective plane, i.e.\ a curve with one vertex that we denote by $c$ and three ends adjacent to $c$ that we call $u$, $v$ and $w$ respectively (see Figure \ref{fig-L}).

