codex
Implemented a verified Track B generator based on the paper’s cycle-closure lattice and spanning-tree minor identity from Definition 2.16 and Proposition 2.24. [Paper PDF](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1303.6478)

Deliverables:

- [gen_1303_6478.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6478/gen_1303_6478.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6478/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6478/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6478/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6478/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1303.6478/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All nine local gates pass.
- Seven adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference algorithm: 1,161,484 exact operations per shipping instance.
- Bare oracle loop: easy 3/3 solved, medium 2/3 solved, hard 0/3 solved.
- Verdict: `hardened` at `n=96`.
- Answer: 12 atoms, 34 characters worst case; intended route: 128 operations.
- Profile corrected to an honest paper-licensed combinatorial/graph reduction.

The hinted and placebo G9 diagnostics were invoked, but OpenRouter’s key limit was exhausted after the bare run. Their four HTTP 403 errors are preserved as script-owned transcripts and are explicitly recorded as unmeasured—not model failures.
